## Primary user (revised)

Built for the owner's **own personal use first** — not a hypothetical generic "language learner" persona. Portfolio narrative describes this same real usage; it is not a separate audience to design for.

## Locked decisions

- **Hero**: Frictionless vocab loop — capture (0–1 taps) → organize → find → study, with AI as a study aid.
- **Dropped**: Daily Discovery, "why today," resurfacing archive, discovery widget, push-for-resurfacing. (**Not the same as** shuffle/random study mode, which is in scope.)
- **Card model**: an item is just **word/phrase + translation**, one field. **`sourceLanguage` auto-detected, optionally set manually at capture when UI allows, or `null` if detection fails and user skips manual pick — not editable after save except one Unsorted resolve.** **`null` → Unsorted.** **`targetLanguage` editable on card.** Folder selection prefills source/target (source locked after prefill).
- **Unsorted resolve (once per card):** Unsorted-only UI — **Move to language folder** (sets `sourceLanguage`) or **Move to custom folder** (files item; may adopt folder source or pick source if folder empty). Normal custom re-file only after resolve or when source is non-null.
- **Translation is never generated automatically — no exceptions**, regardless of target language, not even at capture. Blank unless provided manually or generated in place via explicit on-demand action. A translation targeting the same language as the source is simply the definition/explanation — not a separate category. Same on-demand-only rule applies to examples and "discover similar phrases."
- **Folders**: every item auto-lands in its **built-in per-language folder** plus **at most one optional custom folder** (manual assignment only in v1). **Default custom folder:** last used or manually chosen; prefilled on in-app add; auto-applied on widget/Share when language matches (`sourceLanguage` empty or equal — otherwise skipped). Custom folder: name required; languages from first item / card sync; delete cascades membership only.
- **Language detection fallback**: **`null` source → "Unsorted"**; user may optionally pick manually at capture when UI allows; **one Unsorted resolve** may set language afterward (Unsorted-only, once per card).
- **Discover similar (AI)**: on-demand button, same-language-only, **requires non-null `sourceLanguage`**, suggests items beyond the user's own vocabulary, user chooses what to save.
- **Generation result presentation**: translation and discover-similar surface **multiple candidates** the user picks from; example generation is **single-result**, saved directly (no picker, deliberately kept simple). **Translation, example, and discover-similar generation require non-null `sourceLanguage`** — manual translation/example entry still allowed on `null`-source cards.
- **Related items** (instant matching): same-language-only, **non-null `sourceLanguage` required**, works offline, over user's own vocabulary, duplicates allowed (no dedup in v1).
- **Duplicates**: no dedup/uniqueness check in v1 (accepted limitation); source word/phrase uniqueness is a v2 candidate.
- **Quick note widget**: Type and save a word without opening the app.
- **No tab navigation**: single navigation stack, no `TabView`. Study is not a top-level destination — it's reached per-folder ("Study this folder") or per-search-result, never a standalone tab.
- **Resume**: last folder viewed (or the root folder list if none) — not scroll position or mid-deck state.
- **Capture goal**: Measurably faster than Quizlet (0–1 taps from widget or Share Extension).
- **AI generation implementation** (on-device vs cloud) is deferred to Technical Design — not a product-doc decision.

## v1 scope (locked)

In: word/phrase capture, Share Extension, Quick note widget, per-language auto-folders, one optional custom folder (manual), unified search (keyword + meaning), related items (own vocabulary), on-demand translation (any target language), on-demand discover-similar, on-demand example sentences (manual or generated), flashcard study (folder/shuffle/search-scoped, no tab), resume last folder viewed.

Out: Daily Discovery / resurfacing feed (narrative, "why today", push), general link/photo archive, tags, markdown editor, graph view, multi-device sync, import/export, social, full language course, chat tutor, embedded chat per card / global (v2), spaced repetition (v2), duplicate detection/merging, custom folder nesting/multi-membership, automatic custom-folder assignment, OCR capture (v2).

## Your job as Tech Lead

- Protect scope. Evaluate every new idea against the hero feature first: **fast capture → vocabulary → study**.
- Do not agree with every suggestion. Push back when it doesn't serve the showcase goal.
- Do not re-introduce resurfacing / “why today” without explicit user decision.
- Advance stages only when Definition of Done is met.
- Flag scope creep, perfectionism, premature optimization, unnecessary tech.
- Leave implementation choices (frameworks, models, APIs) to **Technical Design** — not locked in product docs.
